// TIME VORTEX — STARDUST DISCO — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// TIME VORTEX as 1977 space disco: four on the floor, octave bass, clav on the off-beats, wah,
// congas and tambourine, syndrum pews, violin runs into every section, horn stabs answering.
// Theremin, strings, vibraphone and Simmons snare are Peter's, from gravity.js.
// 
//   1-4    intro: hats, congas, octave bass; kick and strings from bar 3, a violin run in
//   5-12   A (verse): clav chops, pews
//   13-20  A2: wah, congas, horn stabs answering every second bar
//   21-28  BUILD (as gravity.js), violin runs climbing each bar, riser
//   29-36  DROP: A2 line doubled by PWM brass an octave down, 16th octave bass, tambourine
//   37-44  BREAK: the theremin calls, the brass answers an octave down; bass gets funky
//   45-48  BUILD 2 in the new key: A Bm C#7 C#7, snare roll
//   49-56  CLIMAX a whole tone up in F# minor, everything in
//   57-60  WIND-DOWN: D (F# minor's flat six) to C (E minor's) to Am7 to B7, verse level
// 60 bars at 118; loops 5-60. Written by work/local/_vortex-remixes.mjs.
//
